Licence:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 maan (see LICENSE in this folder)

OpenDLSS-NR is a third-party, unofficial re-implementation of NVIDIA's DLSS 5 neural rendering network. It is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by NVIDIA Corporation, and neither is Lumina. "DLSS" is a trademark of
NVIDIA Corporation; it appears here only in the upstream project's name. upstream/NOTICE is the upstream project's
own notice, unchanged.

This folder contains source code only. It contains no model weights, no NVIDIA software, headers, binaries or
documentation, no tool that extracts, converts or downloads model weights, and no instructions for obtaining any.
The network runs only on a model folder the user supplies; whoever supplies it is responsible for the licences
that apply to it.

Not vendored: the PTX kernels and their Python generators (scripts/ptx, VK_NV_cuda_kernel_launch), the dlss5vk
tool, the CPU reference, the parity fixtures code, the demo (Filament patch, scenes, ImGui), the WebGPU port, the
build and fetch scripts, the documentation images.
